<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS - Australian company profits rise in Sept qtr.</title>
<headline>RTRS - Australian company profits rise in Sept qtr.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pre-tax profits of Australian companies with more than 30 employees rose 0.3 percent in the September quarter to A$10.536 billion from a downwardly revised A$10.504 billion (revised from A$11.175 billion) in the June quarter, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>This compares with A$10.915 billion a year earlier.</p>
<p>Figures are seasonally-adjusted and before tax, interest and depreciation.  </p>
<p>Company profits before income tax, net interest paid and depreciation --</p>
<p>			     (All figures in A$ million)</p>
<p>			     Sept qtr 96  June qtr 96 Sept qtr 95</p>
<p>    Seasonally adjusted    10,536     10,504     10,915</p>
<p>    Unadjusted		 11,163	9,857     11,494</p>
<p>    Trend Estimates	  10,553     10,691     10,796</p>
<p>	   (Seasonally-adjusted, profits before income tax)</p>
<p>    Mining			1,237	1,548	1,478</p>
<p>    Manufacturing	     2,288	1,884	2,825</p>
<p>    Construction		  102	  129	   52</p>
<p>			     Sept qtr 96  June qtr 96 Sept qtr 95</p>
<p>    Wholesale trade	    517	  632	  639</p>
<p>    Retail trade		 390	  365	  446</p>
<p>    Transport, storage	 144	  -49	  197</p>
<p>    Finance,insurance svcs   185	  202	  157</p>
<p>    Property,business svcs  -105	   81	  107</p>
<p>    Other services	     482	  437	  579</p>
<p>    Total			 5,240	5,228	6,481</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
